          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There are various different paradigms for the interpretation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate+logic"} predicate logic
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            = succeed "-paradigm," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} inhabited type
          %p
            By contrast, in the paradigm that may be called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+some+types"} propositions as some types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            this is called being of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-level+1"} h-level 1
            or being a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} (-1)-type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of type theory, such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of various kinds of categories.
          %p
            Under “propositions as types”, all type-theoretic operations represent corresponding logical operations (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            and
            = succeed "(" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunction
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/or"} or
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} (-1)-truncation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-level+1"} h-level 1-projection
            %strong bracket type
            (when denoted
            = succeed ");" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            it can be identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi isInhab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isInhab
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#AsHigherInductiveType As a higher inductive type
          %p
            In any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %strong support
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(A)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isInhab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isInhab(A)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_{-1} A
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \| A \|_{-1}
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \| A \|
            or, lastly,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [A]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"} higher inductive type
            defined by the two constructors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi isinhab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a \colon A \;\vdash \; isinhab(a) \colon supp(A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi inpath
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  x \colon supp(A) \;,\; y \colon supp(A)
                  \\;\vdash \;
                  inpath(x,y) \colon (x = y)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where in the last
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequent"} sequent
            on the right we have the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Voevodsky"} Voevodsky
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#1Lab"} 1Lab
          %p
            This says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(A)
            is the type which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal
            with the property that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            map to it and that any two term of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            become
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+homotopy+type+theory"} equivalent
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(A)
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            this is
          %pre
            %code
              :preserve
                data isinhab {i : Level} (A : Set i) : Set i where
                  inhab : A → isinhab A
                  inhab-path : (x y : isinhab A) → x ≡ y          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion+principle"} recursion principle
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(A)
            says that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
            and we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi supp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : supp(A) \to B
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi isinhab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(isinhab(a)) \equiv f(a)
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            already follows from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(A)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} supp(A)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction+principle"} induction principle
            states that if we have a family of mere propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(x)
            indexed by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            and we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi isinhab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\prod_{x:A} B(isinhab(x))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo :
                      %mi supp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:\prod_{z:supp(A)} B(z)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi isinhab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(isinhab(a)) \equiv f(a)
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
          %h4#inference_rules Inference rules
          %p The inference rules for bracket types are as follows:
          %ul
            %li Formation rules for bracket types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash [A] \; \mathrm{type}}
          %ul
            %li Introduction rules for bracket types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash [x]:[A] \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} trunc
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:[A], y:[A] \vdash \mathrm{trunc}_A(x, y):x =_{[A]} y \; \mathrm{type}}
          %ul
            %li Elimination rules for bracket types:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo :
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi z
                          %mo :
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi z
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msubsup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ind
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:A \vdash B(x) \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:B(x)} \prod_{z:B(x)} y =_{B(x)} z \quad \Gamma \vdash f:\prod_{x:A} B([x])}{\Gamma, x:[A] \vdash \mathrm{ind}_{[A]}^{B(-)}(p, f, x):B(x)}
          %ul
            %li Computation rules for bracket types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
