          %h2#references References
          %p The original articles are
          %ul
            %li
              M.E. Maietti,
              %em The Type Theory of Categorical Universes
              PhD thesis, Università Degli Studi di Padova, 1998
          %p (which speaks of “mono types”) and
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Pfenning"}> Frank Pfenning
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Intensionality, extensionality, and proof irrelevance in modal type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"}> Steve Awodey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"} Andrej Bauer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Propositions as
                    = succeed "Types" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %strong 14
                (2004) 447-471 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/logcom/14.4.447"}> doi:10.1093/logcom/14.4.447
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://andrej.com/papers/brackets_letter.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , §3.7
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Shulman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em Minicourse on homotopy type theory
              (2012) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/"}> web
              )
          %p Formalization:
          %ul
            %li#Voevodsky
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"}> Vladimir Voevodsky
                ,
                %em The hProp version of the “inhabited” construction.
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/~vladimir/Foundations_library/hProp.html#lab140"}> web
                )
            %li#1Lab
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1lab"}> 1lab
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://1lab.dev/1Lab.HIT.Truncation.html"} Propositional truncation
          %p
            Discussion in the more general context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncation+modality"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-truncations
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Guillaume+Brunerie"}> Guillaume Brunerie
              ,
              %em Truncations and truncated higher inductive types
              (
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/2012/09/16/truncations-and-truncated-higher-inductive-types/"}> web
              )
          %p
            More on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of propositional truncation:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Kraus"}> Nicolai Kraus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The General Universal Property of the Propositional Truncation
              %em TYPES 2014
              Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs)
              %strong 39
              (2015) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.2682"}> arXiv:1411.2682
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.TYPES.2014.111"} doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.TYPES.2014.111
          %p For propositional truncations as sequential colimits, see section 26.5 of
          %ul
            %li#RijkeDraft22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
              (2022),
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/martinescardo/HoTTEST-Summer-School/main/HoTT/hott-intro.pdf"} pdf
          %p as well as section 16.2 of the lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"}> Egbert Rijke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The homotopy image of a map
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Homotopy+Type+Theory"} Introduction to Homotopy Type Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/erijke/hott/hott_intro.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Rijke-IntroductionHoTT-2018.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.andrew.cmu.edu/user/erijke/hott/"} webpage
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncations"} n-truncations
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizations"} localizations
            at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+types"} sphere types
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Jaz+Myers"}> David Jaz Myers
              , Orbifolds as microlinear types in synthetic differential cohesive homotopy type theory (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.15887"}> arXiv:2205.15887
              )
          %p
            That propositional truncations with judgmental computation rules along with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+booleans"} type of booleans
            imply function extensionality:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Kraus"}> Nicolai Kraus
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"} Martín Escardó
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"} Thierry Coquand
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thorsten+Altenkirch"} Thorsten Altenkirch
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notions of Anonymous Existence in Martin-Löf Type Theory
              %strong 13
              1 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.23638/LMCS-13(1:15)2017"}> doi:10.23638/LMCS-13(1:15)2017
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.03346"} arXiv:1610.03346
